# `{{.Resource}}` CRUD module

`weld add crud {{.Resource}}` generated this resource once. weld records every
file in `weld.json` and never regenerates it, so edit freely.

## Files

| File | Holds |
|---|---|
| `db/migrations/<version>_create_{{.Table}}.sql` | The `{{.Table}}` table. |
| `db/query/{{.Table}}.sql` | The sqlc statements. Run `weld gen sqlc` after editing. |
| `internal/data/{{.Resource}}_repo.go` | `data.{{.Title}}Repository` and its PostgreSQL implementation. |
| `internal/data/{{.Resource}}_repo_integration_test.go` | Runs against a configured test database only. |
| `dto.go` | Wire types and the shared field rules (`validateInput`). |
| `service.go` | `Service`, `NewService` (bound by the Loom graph), `NewServiceWith`, `NewDemoService`. |
| `memory.go` | The in-memory repository the demo service and the tests use. |
| `module.go` / `handler.go` | The route table and the handlers. |

## Routes

Paths are relative to the module prefix, `httpserver.ModulePrefix("{{.Resource}}")`
(`/api/{{.Resource}}` by default).

| Route | Policy | Answer |
|---|---|---|
| `GET {prefix}?limit=&offset=` | public | one page and the total (`limit` defaults to 50, at most 200) |
| `GET {prefix}/{id}` | public | the {{.Resource}}, or 404 |
| `POST {prefix}` | admin | 201 and the stored {{.Resource}} |
| `PUT {prefix}/{id}` | admin | the updated {{.Resource}}, or 404 |
| `DELETE {prefix}/{id}` | admin | 204, or 404 |

The admin policy is a name: `internal/di/http_policies.go` decides what it
means, and the default guard denies everything until you wire authentication.

## Fields

{{range .Fields}}- `{{.Column}}` — `{{.SQLType}}` / `{{.GoType}}`
{{end}}
To add a column: write a new migration (`weld db create add_<column>_to_{{.Table}}`),
add it to the statements in `db/query/{{.Table}}.sql`, run `weld gen sqlc`, then
extend `data.{{.Title}}`, `data.{{.Title}}Input`, the DTOs and `memory.go`.
The compiler points at every place that needs the new field.

## Running it

`NewService` takes the database pool, so serving this module needs the database
settings in `config.yml`. Apply the migration with `weld db migrate up`, or turn
on `database.auto_migrate`.
